│ leadership, a strong position, and greater firepower". One Texian was        │
│ injured, and Richard Andrews became the first Texian soldier to die in       │
│ battle. Between 14 and 76 Mexican soldiers were killed. Historian Stephen    │
│ Hardin believes that "the relative ease of the victory at Concepción         │
│ instilled in the Texians a reliance on their long rifles and a contempt for  │
│ their enemies", which may have led to the later Texian defeat at Coleto.,    │
│ Victor: T.                                                                   │
